<title>AUSTRIA: AMS reports 1996 net loss, dividend down.</title>
<headline>AMS reports 1996 net loss, dividend down.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for the year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of schillings unless stated)</p>
<p>						1996	   1995</p>
<p> Group sales			    1,793.9	1,886.5</p>
<p> Group operating			  75.1 loss    293.2</p>
<p> Group pre-tax			    100.6 loss   266.9</p>
<p> Group net				   52.0	  200.5</p>
<p> Group net after minority interests 105.6 loss   188.4</p>
<p> Dividend (schillings)		   10	     12</p>
<p> Group personnel expenses	     718.0	  493.2</p>
<p> Group depreciation		     356.0	  206.6</p>
<p>NOTE - AMS said in a statement group sales in the first quarter 1997 fell to 344.9 million schillings from 572.8 million in the year-ago period. Order entry rose to 499.4 million schillings from 405.3 million and order backlog fell to 574.7 million from 869.9</p>
<p>NOTE - AMS said the group was &quot;prepared for solid growth in 1997&quot; after 1996 figures that were below expectations. -- Vienna newsroom, +43-1 531 12 254</p>
</text>
